+- Assigning to a property a shape or a formatting object does not have is accepted silently: there
+  is no `__setattr__` override or `__slots__` restriction anywhere in the installed package, so the
+  unknown attribute is simply stored on the instance and reads back exactly as assigned — no
+  `AttributeError`, no validation, and nothing reported. A misspelt property name therefore fails
+  silently rather than being caught: the typo creates a harmless, unused extra attribute instead of
+  raising an error, and the shape or format's real state is left unchanged.
